-- title:
--   Definitions for Classification of 3-graded causal subalgebras of real simple Lie algebras
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Classification of 3-graded causal subalgebras of real simple Lie algebras* (arXiv:2001.03125) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `DirectThree`: Independent internal three-piece sum, pp. 1, 4.
--   - `adSpace`: Real adjoint eigenspace, notation on p. 4.
--   - `Hyperbolic`: A genuine diagonal decomposition into real eigenspaces, Remark 2.5, p. 6.
--   - `complexSpectrum`: Complex spectrum of a real operator, in real/imaginary coordinates on its complexification. The two equations express T(u+iv)=z(u+iv). This is the full complex spectrum, not only the set of real eigenvalues; finite dimension is used throughout.
--   - `fiveSpectrum`: The five possible spectral values in Section 3.2, p. 21.
--   - `ThreeGrading`: A nonzero element inducing this decomposition is required separately, Lemma 2.6, p. 6.
--   - `expEnd`: The convergent operator exponential in the usual topology, pp. 1, 4.
--   - `LineFreeAdmissible`: Admissibility is existence of a generating line-free closed convex invariant SET, Definition 2.1, p. 4. Translation stabilizers implement the source's H(C), without replacing admissibility by a condition on simple factors.
--   - `HermitianSimple`: Hermitian simple by the equivalent invariant proper-cone definition, Section 2.2, p. 5.
--   - `MinimalCone`: Chosen orientation of the minimal invariant cone, pp. 2, 5–6.
--   - `maximalCone`: Negative Killing dual with the orientation on pp. 5–6.
--   - `Cartan`: Cartan involution through positive definiteness of -B(x,theta y), pp. 6, 9.
--   - `autoSpace`: Simultaneous eigenspaces use the actual given automorphisms, p. 4.
--   - `Abelian`: Abelian subspaces are real linear subspaces, p. 6.
--   - `MaximalAbelianIn`: Maximality inside the specified ambient subspace, pp. 6, 18.
--   - `RestrictedRoot`: The actual restricted-root eigenspaces, equation (4), p. 6.
--   - `rootsC`: Standard C_r root set in the dual of a chosen basis, equation (4), p. 6.
--   - `rootsBC`: Standard nonreduced BC_r adds the short roots, equation (5), p. 6.
--   - `RestrictedTubeType`: Tube type is defined by the restricted roots, not by Lemma 2.6's conclusion, p. 6.
--   - `realRank`: Real split rank. The set contains zero and is bounded by dim G, so sSup has neither the empty-set nor the unbounded-set default, pp. 6, 25–29.
--   - `InnerFixed`: Inner automorphisms generated by elements fixed by tau, pp. 18, 27.
--   - `CompatiblePair`: The pair A(g), equation (10), pp. 18–19.
--   - `derivationSlice`: Closed causal cone slices for a general derivation, introduction p. 1.
--   - `causalSlice`: Causal slices for D=ad h, pp. 1, 17–18.
--   - `causalAlgebra`: Lie algebra generated by the two causal cones, abstract p. 1. Defined for ALL W; its three-piece formula is asserted only with the source's additional hypotheses.
--   - `coneSlice`: Without tau, the two signed W-slices in Lemma 3.2 and Theorem 3.9, pp. 18, 21.
--   - `sliceAlgebra`: The generated algebra s(h), recomputed from W and h, Theorem 3.9, p. 21.
--   - `tubeAlgebra`: The generated algebra g_t(h) from the full extreme eigenspaces, p. 21.
--   - `gradingSign`: The sign involution on an actual three-grading, exp(i*pi*ad h)=1-2(ad h)^2, Section 3.1, p. 19. Used only with ThreeGrading h.
--   - `CayleyType`: Symmetric dual isomorphism, Definition 2.18, p. 10. The target's coordinates are g^tau + i g^-tau; the bracket's imaginary-square sign is negative.
--   - `OrdinaryRootVector`: Complex root vectors in real coordinates, Section 2.1, p. 4.
--   - `OrdinaryRoot`: Ordinary roots of (g_C,t_C), determined by their restrictions to t, p. 4.
--   - `CompactRoot`: Compactness means containment of the WHOLE complex root space in k_C, p. 4.
--   - `AdaptedPositiveSystem`: Positive systems and adaptedness use X=iH in i*t, so a(X)=-Im(a(H)), p. 4. The reality condition is explicit; compactly embedded Cartans ensure it in applications.
--   - `rootConeGenerators`: Real generators i[Z,conj Z]=2[u,v] of C_min, Section 2.1, p. 5. Only noncompact positive roots are used, and generators are actual elements of t.
--   - `printedMinimalRootCone`: Literal printed C_min, p. 5. The printed C_min/C_max signs conflict on sl2. No compatible-pair or central-projection assertion is made here.
--   - `printedMaximalRootCone`: Literal printed C_max, p. 5. Kept separate from printedMinimalRootCone because the source signs conflict under the ordinary-root convention.
--   - `printedRootConeDualInterior`: Dual interior of the LITERAL printed cone, in the finite-dimensional continuous real dual. This is not a central projection and does not resolve the supporting-paper objective.
--   - `printedCentralRootCone`: The central intersection of the literal root cone, in the REAL center. The source of this additional interface is arXiv:2007.13445v1, Theorem 2.11, PDF p. 8. It is an intersection, not a projection. The unresolved printed root-cone sign remains.
--   - `printedCentralRootDualInterior`: Dual interior of the printed central intersection, in the usual real dual topology. This definition is literal only; no compatibility or admissibility theorem is asserted.
--   - `EuclideanJordan`: Finite-dimensional unital euclidean Jordan data, Definition 2.22, p. 11. The scalar product is real, symmetric, positive definite and associative.
--   - `JordanAuto`: Jordan automorphisms preserve the product, not just the underlying vector space, p. 15.
--   - `Idempotent`: Idempotency, Definition 2.26(a), p. 12.
--   - `PrimitiveIn`: Primitivity RELATIVE to a subalgebra S; zero is excluded, p. 13.
--   - `FrameIn`: Frames in subalgebras with their partial units, Definition 2.26, pp. 12–13.
--   - `JordanFrame`: A frame of V uses the actual unit, p. 13.
--   - `HasJordanRank`: Rank through an actual frame, avoiding a default-valued choice of rank on bad inputs, p. 13.
--   - `SimpleJordanIn`: Genuine Jordan ideals and nontriviality, Definition 2.22(c), p. 11.
--   - `squares`: The closed square cone is a set of actual products, pp. 12, 19.
--   - `jordanOmega`: Omega_V is OPEN; its closure is used in Lemma 2.28, pp. 12–13.
--   - `peirce`: Peirce eigenspaces, Definition 2.22(e), p. 11.
--   - `jordanFixed`: Fixed Jordan subalgebra, pp. 15–17.
--   - `JordanSplit`: JordanSplit is equality of the two frame ranks, Definition 2.34(a), p. 15.
--   - `NonSplit`: Non-split is the rank doubling condition, not the absence of fixed frame entries, p. 15.
--   - `jordanQuadratic`: Quadratic representation P(w), Definition 2.22(d), p. 11.
--   - `PeirceReflection`: The defining reflection is P(2c-e), not P(c), Definition 2.34(b), p. 15.
--   - `partialUnit`: Ordered partial frame sum, pp. 14, 17. Defined also for k=0.
--   - `pairedFrame`: The first s paired idempotents; only s entries, Lemma 2.41, p. 17.
--   - `fixedLie`: Fixed Lie algebra with the ambient bracket, notation p. 4.
--   - `CartanHElement`: H-element in the chosen Cartan decomposition, pp. 5, 8–9.
--   - `minimalConeAt`: The smallest invariant proper cone containing the specified H-element, pp. 5–6. The family is nonempty on H-elements in hermitian simple algebras.
--   - `KKTModel`: Product, unit, and scalar product of Example 2.23, p. 12. For eigenvalue d=2 the triple is (h,e,y); for d=1 it is (2h,e,y). The Jordan operations are pinned to this chosen triple, rather than left unrelated.
--   - `FullRankTube`: The complete full-rank tube-subalgebra properties of Corollary 3.20, p. 28.
--   - `FiveGrading`: The five-term diagonal grading; distinct real eigenvalues make the summands independent, Lemma 3.24, p. 29. No nonzero half-eigenspace is silently required.
--   - `CayleyCoordinates`: The chosen normalized Cartan basis in Section 3.1, p. 19.
--   - `coordinateH`: H=(1/2)sum H_i of Section 3.1, p. 19.
--   - `coefficientElement`: The element with coefficients lambda_i, Proposition 3.5, p. 19.
--   - `cutElement`: The specified coefficient cutoff, not a freely chosen h', Proposition 3.5, p. 19.
--   - `CayleyJordanFrame`: The actual chosen Jordan frame of Examples 2.27 and Remark 2.29, pp. 13–14, 19. The multiplication-root relation fixes its normalization and identifies the frame with H_i. The orientation is exactly the Wmin cap V = closed square cone convention of Section 3.1.
--   - `OrthogonalReal`: Concrete REAL indefinite orthogonal matrix algebra, Definition 2.35 and pp. 26–28. The signature has p positive and q negative diagonal entries.
--   - `SpinSpace`: The spin factor R x R^n, Example 2.35, pp. 15–16.
--   - `spinProduct`: The actual spin-factor Jordan product, Example 2.35, p. 15.
--   - `SpinIsomorphic`: Jordan-algebra isomorphism, with the induced product on the specified subalgebra. The image of the product must exist IN S and map to the explicit spin product.
--   - `SpinRealization`: The chosen h, KKT product, and -tau fixed spin factor in Remark 3.21, p. 28.
--   - `complexScalePair`: Real-coordinate scalar multiplication on the actual complexification, Section 2.1, p. 4.
--   - `complexConjugatePair`: Conjugation relative to the real form, pp. 4–5.
--   - `complexBracketPair`: Scalar-extended bracket, pp. 4–5.
--   - `extendRoot`: The complex-linear extension of a real restriction a:t -> C, Section 2.1, p. 4.
-- source:
--   Classification of 3-graded causal subalgebras of real simple Lie algebras, arXiv:2001.03125v2, https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.03125v2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Frontier30_P26

/-! Daniel Oeh, arXiv:2001.03125v2. Paper-local definitions and statement drafts.
Reused cone and inner-action definitions come from the pinned accepted Frontier30.P26 module.
Concrete classification tables are deferred explicitly in HARD.md; no symbolic type labels
stand in for concrete Lie or Jordan algebras. Compilation is pending the batch handoff. -/

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Next46.P05

noncomputable section

open Set
open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Frontier30.P26
  (bracketSpan innerWord Invariant ClosedCone GeneratingInvariantCone CompactlyEmbedded)
open scoped BigOperators

attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable Classical.decEq
attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

/-- Usual finite-dimensional real topology, using a norm on the original additive group. -/
local instance lieNormedGroup (G : Type*) [LieRing G] [LieAlgebra ℝ G]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ G] : NormedAddCommGroup G :=
  NormedAddCommGroup.induced G (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ G) → ℝ)
    (Module.finBasis ℝ G).equivFun.toLinearMap (Module.finBasis ℝ G).equivFun.injective

/-- The norm uses the original scalar action, so the Lie and topological structures agree. -/
local instance lieNormedSpace (G : Type*) [LieRing G] [LieAlgebra ℝ G]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ G] : NormedSpace ℝ G :=
  NormedSpace.induced ℝ G (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ G) → ℝ)
    (Module.finBasis ℝ G).equivFun.toLinearMap

section LieDefinitions

variable {G : Type*} [LieRing G] [LieAlgebra ℝ G] [FiniteDimensional ℝ G]

/-- Independent internal three-piece sum, pp. 1, 4. -/
def DirectThree (S A B C : Submodule ℝ G) : Prop :=
  S = A ⊔ B ⊔ C ∧ Disjoint A B ∧ Disjoint (A ⊔ B) C

/-- Real adjoint eigenspace, notation on p. 4. -/
def adSpace (h : G) (t : ℝ) : Submodule ℝ G :=
  Module.End.eigenspace (LieAlgebra.ad ℝ G h) t

/-- A genuine diagonal decomposition into real eigenspaces, Remark 2.5, p. 6. -/
def Hyperbolic (h : G) : Prop := (⨆ t : ℝ, adSpace h t) = ⊤

/-- Complex spectrum of a real operator, in real/imaginary coordinates on its complexification.
The two equations express T(u+iv)=z(u+iv). This is the full complex spectrum, not
only the set of real eigenvalues; finite dimension is used throughout. -/
def complexSpectrum (T : G →ₗ[ℝ] G) : Set ℂ :=
  {z | ∃ u v : G, (u ≠ 0 ∨ v ≠ 0) ∧
    T u = z.re • u - z.im • v ∧ T v = z.im • u + z.re • v}

/-- The five possible spectral values in Section 3.2, p. 21. -/
def fiveSpectrum : Set ℂ := {0, (1 / 2 : ℂ), -(1 / 2 : ℂ), 1, -1}

/-- A nonzero element inducing this decomposition is required separately, Lemma 2.6, p. 6. -/
def ThreeGrading (h : G) : Prop :=
  DirectThree ⊤ (adSpace h (-1)) (adSpace h 0) (adSpace h 1)

/-- The convergent operator exponential in the usual topology, pp. 1, 4. -/
def expEnd (T : G →ₗ[ℝ] G) : G →L[ℝ] G :=
  NormedSpace.exp (LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap T)

/-- Admissibility is existence of a generating line-free closed convex invariant SET,
Definition 2.1, p. 4. Translation stabilizers implement the source's H(C), without
replacing admissibility by a condition on simple factors. -/
def LineFreeAdmissible : Prop :=
  ∃ C : Set G, C.Nonempty ∧ IsClosed C ∧ Convex ℝ C ∧ Invariant C ∧
    Submodule.span ℝ C = ⊤ ∧
    ∀ x : G, (fun c => c + x) '' C = C → x = 0

/-- Hermitian simple by the equivalent invariant proper-cone definition, Section 2.2, p. 5. -/
def HermitianSimple : Prop :=
  LieAlgebra.IsSimple ℝ G ∧ ∃ W : Set G, GeneratingInvariantCone W

/-- Chosen orientation of the minimal invariant cone, pp. 2, 5–6. -/
def MinimalCone (W : Set G) : Prop :=
  GeneratingInvariantCone W ∧ ∀ C : Set G, GeneratingInvariantCone C →
    W ⊆ C ∨ W ⊆ Neg.neg '' C

/-- Negative Killing dual with the orientation on pp. 5–6. -/
def maximalCone (W : Set G) : Set G :=
  {x | ∀ y ∈ W, killingForm ℝ G x y ≤ 0}

/-- Cartan involution through positive definiteness of -B(x,theta y), pp. 6, 9. -/
def Cartan (theta : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) : Prop :=
  Function.Involutive theta ∧ ∀ x : G, x ≠ 0 →
    killingForm ℝ G x (theta x) < 0

/-- Simultaneous eigenspaces use the actual given automorphisms, p. 4. -/
def autoSpace (tau : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) (t : ℝ) : Submodule ℝ G :=
  Module.End.eigenspace tau.toLinearEquiv.toLinearMap t

/-- Abelian subspaces are real linear subspaces, p. 6. -/
def Abelian (A : Submodule ℝ G) : Prop := ∀ x ∈ A, ∀ y ∈ A, ⁅x, y⁆ = 0

/-- Maximality inside the specified ambient subspace, pp. 6, 18. -/
def MaximalAbelianIn (A P : Submodule ℝ G) : Prop :=
  A ≤ P ∧ Abelian A ∧ ∀ B : Submodule ℝ G, B ≤ P → Abelian B → A ≤ B → B ≤ A

/-- The actual restricted-root eigenspaces, equation (4), p. 6. -/
def RestrictedRoot (A : Submodule ℝ G) (a : A →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) : Prop :=
  a ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ x : G, x ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ H : A, ⁅(H : G), x⁆ = a H • x

/-- Standard C_r root set in the dual of a chosen basis, equation (4), p. 6. -/
def rootsC {r : ℕ} {A : Submodule ℝ G} (b : Module.Basis (Fin r) ℝ A) : Set (A →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) :=
  {a | (∃ i, a = 2 • b.coord i ∨ a = -(2 • b.coord i)) ∨
    ∃ i j, i ≠ j ∧ (a = b.coord i + b.coord j ∨ a = b.coord i - b.coord j ∨
      a = -(b.coord i + b.coord j) ∨ a = -(b.coord i - b.coord j))}

/-- Standard nonreduced BC_r adds the short roots, equation (5), p. 6. -/
def rootsBC {r : ℕ} {A : Submodule ℝ G} (b : Module.Basis (Fin r) ℝ A) : Set (A →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) :=
  rootsC b ∪ {a | ∃ i, a = b.coord i ∨ a = -b.coord i}

/-- Tube type is defined by the restricted roots, not by Lemma 2.6's conclusion, p. 6. -/
def RestrictedTubeType : Prop :=
  ∃ theta : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G, Cartan theta ∧ ∃ A : Submodule ℝ G,
    MaximalAbelianIn A (autoSpace theta (-1)) ∧ ∃ r : ℕ, 0 < r ∧
      ∃ b : Module.Basis (Fin r) ℝ A, {a | RestrictedRoot A a} = rootsC b

/-- Real split rank. The set contains zero and is bounded by dim G, so sSup has
neither the empty-set nor the unbounded-set default, pp. 6, 25–29. -/
def realRank : ℕ :=
  sSup {n | ∃ A : Submodule ℝ G, Abelian A ∧
    (∀ x ∈ A, Hyperbolic x) ∧ Module.finrank ℝ A = n}

/-- Inner automorphisms generated by elements fixed by tau, pp. 18, 27. -/
def InnerFixed (tau phi : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) : Prop :=
  ∃ xs : List G, (∀ x ∈ xs, tau x = x) ∧ ∀ x : G, innerWord xs x = phi x

/-- The pair A(g), equation (10), pp. 18–19. -/
def CompatiblePair (W : Set G) (tau theta : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) : Prop :=
  Function.Involutive tau ∧ Cartan theta ∧ tau '' W = Neg.neg '' W ∧
    ∀ x : G, theta (tau x) = tau (theta x)

/-- Closed causal cone slices for a general derivation, introduction p. 1. -/
def derivationSlice (W : Set G) (tau : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) (D : G →ₗ[ℝ] G) (t : ℝ) : Set G :=
  {x | x ∈ (fun w => t • w) '' W ∧ tau x = -x ∧ D x = t • x}

/-- Causal slices for D=ad h, pp. 1, 17–18. -/
def causalSlice (W : Set G) (tau : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) (h : G) (t : ℝ) : Set G :=
  derivationSlice W tau (LieAlgebra.ad ℝ G h) t

/-- Lie algebra generated by the two causal cones, abstract p. 1. Defined for ALL W;
its three-piece formula is asserted only with the source's additional hypotheses. -/
def causalAlgebra (W : Set G) (tau : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) (h : G) : LieSubalgebra ℝ G :=
  LieSubalgebra.lieSpan ℝ G (causalSlice W tau h (-1) ∪ causalSlice W tau h 1)

/-- Without tau, the two signed W-slices in Lemma 3.2 and Theorem 3.9, pp. 18, 21. -/
def coneSlice (W : Set G) (h : G) (t : ℝ) : Set G :=
  (fun w => t • w) '' W ∩ (adSpace h t : Set G)

/-- The generated algebra s(h), recomputed from W and h, Theorem 3.9, p. 21. -/
def sliceAlgebra (W : Set G) (h : G) : LieSubalgebra ℝ G :=
  LieSubalgebra.lieSpan ℝ G (coneSlice W h (-1) ∪ coneSlice W h 1)

/-- The generated algebra g_t(h) from the full extreme eigenspaces, p. 21. -/
def tubeAlgebra (h : G) : LieSubalgebra ℝ G :=
  LieSubalgebra.lieSpan ℝ G ((adSpace h (-1) : Set G) ∪ (adSpace h 1 : Set G))

/-- The sign involution on an actual three-grading, exp(i*pi*ad h)=1-2(ad h)^2,
Section 3.1, p. 19. Used only with ThreeGrading h. -/
def gradingSign (h x : G) : G := x - (2 : ℝ) • ⁅h, ⁅h, x⁆⁆

/-- Symmetric dual isomorphism, Definition 2.18, p. 10. The target's coordinates
are g^tau + i g^-tau; the bracket's imaginary-square sign is negative. -/
def CayleyType (tau : G ≃ₗ⁅ℝ⁆ G) : Prop :=
  ∃ f : G ≃ₗ[ℝ] (autoSpace tau 1 × autoSpace tau (-1)),
    (∀ x y : G,
      ((f ⁅x, y⁆).1 : G) = ⁅((f x).1 : G), ((f y).1 : G)⁆ -
        ⁅((f x).2 : G), ((f y).2 : G)⁆ ∧
      ((f ⁅x, y⁆).2 : G) = ⁅((f x).1 : G), ((f y).2 : G)⁆ +
        ⁅((f x).2 : G), ((f y).1 : G)⁆) ∧
    ∀ x : G, ((f (tau x)).1 : G) = ((f x).1 : G) ∧
      ((f (tau x)).2 : G) = -((f x).2 : G)

/-- Complex root vectors in real coordinates, Section 2.1, p. 4. -/
def OrdinaryRootVector (T : Submodule ℝ G) (a : T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ) (z : G × G) : Prop :=
  ∀ H : T, ⁅(H : G), z.1⁆ = (a H).re • z.1 - (a H).im • z.2 ∧
    ⁅(H : G), z.2⁆ = (a H).im • z.1 + (a H).re • z.2

/-- Ordinary roots of (g_C,t_C), determined by their restrictions to t, p. 4. -/
def OrdinaryRoot (T : Submodule ℝ G) (a : T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ) : Prop :=
  a ≠ 0 ∧ ∃ z : G × G, z ≠ 0 ∧ OrdinaryRootVector T a z

/-- Compactness means containment of the WHOLE complex root space in k_C, p. 4. -/
def CompactRoot (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (a : T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ) : Prop :=
  OrdinaryRoot T a ∧ ∀ z, OrdinaryRootVector T a z → z.1 ∈ K ∧ z.2 ∈ K

/-- Positive systems and adaptedness use X=iH in i*t, so a(X)=-Im(a(H)), p. 4.
The reality condition is explicit; compactly embedded Cartans ensure it in applications. -/
def AdaptedPositiveSystem (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) : Prop :=
  ∃ H : T,
    (∀ a, OrdinaryRoot T a → (a H).re = 0 ∧ (a H).im ≠ 0) ∧
    P = {a | OrdinaryRoot T a ∧ 0 < -(a H).im} ∧
    ∀ a, CompactRoot K T a → ∀ b ∈ P, ¬ CompactRoot K T b →
      -(a H).im < -(b H).im

/-- Real generators i[Z,conj Z]=2[u,v] of C_min, Section 2.1, p. 5.
Only noncompact positive roots are used, and generators are actual elements of t. -/
def rootConeGenerators (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) : Set T :=
  {H | ∃ a ∈ P, ¬ CompactRoot K T a ∧ ∃ z : G × G,
    OrdinaryRootVector T a z ∧ (H : G) = (2 : ℝ) • ⁅z.1, z.2⁆}

/-- Literal printed C_min, p. 5. The printed C_min/C_max signs conflict on sl2.
No compatible-pair or central-projection assertion is made here. -/
def printedMinimalRootCone (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) : Set T :=
  ⋂₀ {C : Set T | IsClosed C ∧ Convex ℝ C ∧ (0 : T) ∈ C ∧
    (∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → ∀ x ∈ C, t • x ∈ C) ∧ rootConeGenerators K T P ⊆ C}

/-- Literal printed C_max, p. 5. Kept separate from printedMinimalRootCone
because the source signs conflict under the ordinary-root convention. -/
def printedMaximalRootCone (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) : Set T :=
  {H | ∀ a ∈ P, ¬ CompactRoot K T a → (a H).re = 0 ∧ 0 ≤ -(a H).im}

/-- Dual interior of the LITERAL printed cone, in the finite-dimensional continuous real dual.
This is not a central projection and does not resolve the supporting-paper objective. -/
def printedRootConeDualInterior (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) :
    Set (T →L[ℝ] ℝ) :=
  interior {f | ∀ H ∈ printedMinimalRootCone K T P, 0 ≤ f H}

/-- The central intersection of the literal root cone, in the REAL center. The source of
this additional interface is arXiv:2007.13445v1, Theorem 2.11, PDF p. 8.
It is an intersection, not a projection. The unresolved printed root-cone sign remains. -/
def printedCentralRootCone (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) :
    Set (LieAlgebra.center ℝ G) :=
  {z | ∃ H : T, (H : G) = (z : G) ∧ H ∈ printedMinimalRootCone K T P}

/-- Dual interior of the printed central intersection, in the usual real dual topology.
This definition is literal only; no compatibility or admissibility theorem is asserted. -/
def printedCentralRootDualInterior (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) :
    Set ((LieAlgebra.center ℝ G) →L[ℝ] ℝ) :=
  interior {f | ∀ z ∈ printedCentralRootCone K T P, 0 ≤ f z}

example (h : G) : (0 : G) ∈ adSpace h 1 := by simp [adSpace]

example (x : G) : innerWord ([] : List G) x = x := rfl

example (T : Submodule ℝ G) (a : T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ) :
    OrdinaryRootVector T a (0, 0) := by
  intro H
  simp

example (K T : Submodule ℝ G) (P : Set (T →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)) :
    (0 : T) ∈ printedMinimalRootCone K T P := by
  apply Set.mem_sInter.mpr
  intro C hC
  exact hC.2.2.1

end LieDefinitions

section JordanDefinitions

variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℝ V]

/-- Finite-dimensional unital euclidean Jordan data, Definition 2.22, p. 11.
The scalar product is real, symmetric, positive definite and associative. -/
structure EuclideanJordan (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℝ V] where
  product : V →ₗ[ℝ] V →ₗ[ℝ] V
  unit : V
  comm : ∀ x y, product x y = product y x
  jordan : ∀ x y, product x (product (product x x) y) =
    product (product x x) (product x y)
  unit_mul : ∀ x, product unit x = x
  scalar : LinearMap.BilinForm ℝ V
  scalar_symm : ∀ x y, scalar x y = scalar y x
  scalar_pos : ∀ x, x ≠ 0 → 0 < scalar x x
  scalar_assoc : ∀ x y z, scalar (product x y) z = scalar y (product x z)

/-- Jordan automorphisms preserve the product, not just the underlying vector space, p. 15. -/
structure JordanAuto (J : EuclideanJordan V) where
  linear : V ≃ₗ[ℝ] V
  map_product : ∀ x y, linear (J.product x y) = J.product (linear x) (linear y)

/-- Idempotency, Definition 2.26(a), p. 12. -/
def Idempotent (J : EuclideanJordan V) (c : V) : Prop := J.product c c = c

/-- Primitivity RELATIVE to a subalgebra S; zero is excluded, p. 13. -/
def PrimitiveIn (J : EuclideanJordan V) (S : Submodule ℝ V) (c : V) : Prop :=
  c ∈ S ∧ c ≠ 0 ∧ Idempotent J c ∧ ∀ a ∈ S, ∀ b ∈ S,
    Idempotent J a → Idempotent J b → J.product a b = 0 → c = a + b → a = 0 ∨ b = 0

/-- Frames in subalgebras with their partial units, Definition 2.26, pp. 12–13. -/
def FrameIn (J : EuclideanJordan V) (S : Submodule ℝ V) (u : V)
    {r : ℕ} (c : Fin r → V) : Prop :=
  (∀ i, PrimitiveIn J S (c i)) ∧ (∀ i j, i ≠ j → J.product (c i) (c j) = 0) ∧
    (∑ i, c i) = u ∧ (∀ x ∈ S, J.product u x = x)

/-- A frame of V uses the actual unit, p. 13. -/
def JordanFrame (J : EuclideanJordan V) {r : ℕ} (c : Fin r → V) : Prop :=
  FrameIn J ⊤ J.unit c

/-- Rank through an actual frame, avoiding a default-valued choice of rank on bad inputs, p. 13. -/
def HasJordanRank (J : EuclideanJordan V) (S : Submodule ℝ V) (u : V) (r : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ c : Fin r → V, FrameIn J S u c

/-- Genuine Jordan ideals and nontriviality, Definition 2.22(c), p. 11. -/
def SimpleJordanIn (J : EuclideanJordan V) (S : Submodule ℝ V) : Prop :=
  S ≠ ⊥ ∧ (∀ x ∈ S, ∀ y ∈ S, J.product x y ∈ S) ∧
    ∀ I : Submodule ℝ V, I ≤ S →
      (∀ x ∈ S, ∀ y ∈ I, J.product x y ∈ I) → I = ⊥ ∨ I = S

/-- The closed square cone is a set of actual products, pp. 12, 19. -/
def squares (J : EuclideanJordan V) : Set V := {y | ∃ x : V, y = J.product x x}

/-- Omega_V is OPEN; its closure is used in Lemma 2.28, pp. 12–13. -/
def jordanOmega [TopologicalSpace V] (J : EuclideanJordan V) : Set V := interior (squares J)

/-- Peirce eigenspaces, Definition 2.22(e), p. 11. -/
def peirce (J : EuclideanJordan V) (c : V) (t : ℝ) : Submodule ℝ V :=
  Module.End.eigenspace (J.product c) t

/-- Fixed Jordan subalgebra, pp. 15–17. -/
def jordanFixed (J : EuclideanJordan V) (a : JordanAuto J) : Submodule ℝ V :=
  Module.End.eigenspace a.linear.toLinearMap 1

/-- JordanSplit is equality of the two frame ranks, Definition 2.34(a), p. 15. -/
def JordanSplit (J : EuclideanJordan V) (a : JordanAuto J) : Prop :=
  ∃ r, HasJordanRank J ⊤ J.unit r ∧ HasJordanRank J (jordanFixed J a) J.unit r

/-- Non-split is the rank doubling condition, not the absence of fixed frame entries, p. 15. -/
def NonSplit (J : EuclideanJordan V) (a : JordanAuto J) : Prop :=
  ∃ s, HasJordanRank J ⊤ J.unit (2 * s) ∧ HasJordanRank J (jordanFixed J a) J.unit s

/-- Quadratic representation P(w), Definition 2.22(d), p. 11. -/
def jordanQuadratic (J : EuclideanJordan V) (w x : V) : V :=
  (2 : ℝ) • J.product w (J.product w x) - J.product (J.product w w) x

/-- The defining reflection is P(2c-e), not P(c), Definition 2.34(b), p. 15. -/
def PeirceReflection (J : EuclideanJordan V) (a : JordanAuto J) : Prop :=
  ∃ c : V, Idempotent J c ∧ ∀ x, a.linear x = jordanQuadratic J ((2 : ℝ) • c - J.unit) x

/-- Ordered partial frame sum, pp. 14, 17. Defined also for k=0. -/
def partialUnit {r : ℕ} (c : Fin r → V) (k : ℕ) : V :=
  ∑ i : Fin r, if i.val < k then c i else 0

/-- The first s paired idempotents; only s entries, Lemma 2.41, p. 17. -/
def pairedFrame {s : ℕ} (c : Fin (2 * s) → V) (a : V → V) : Fin s → V :=
  fun i => c ⟨i.val, by omega⟩ + a (c ⟨i.val, by omega⟩)

example (J : EuclideanJordan V) (x : V) : J.product J.unit x = x := J.unit_mul x

example (J : EuclideanJordan V) (x : V) :
    jordanQuadratic J J.unit x = x := by
  simp only [jordanQuadratic, J.unit_mul, two_smul]
  abel

example (J : EuclideanJordan V) : (0 : V) ∈ squares J := by
  exact ⟨0, by simp⟩

example {r : ℕ} (c : Fin r → V) : partialUnit c 0 = 0 := by
  simp [partialUnit]

example (J : EuclideanJordan V) (S : Submodule ℝ V) : ¬ PrimitiveIn J S 0 := by
  intro h
  exact h.2.1 rfl

end JordanDefinitions

